  "title": { "en": "Work and study", "uz": "Ish va o'qish", "ru": "Работа и учёба", "tr": "İş ve eğitim" },
  "goal": {
    "en": "Talk about jobs, workplaces and studies, and say what other people do.",
    "uz": "Kasblar, ish joyi va o'qish haqida gapiring, boshqalar nima ish qilishini ayting.",
    "ru": "Расскажите о профессиях, работе и учёбе и о том, чем занимаются другие люди.",
    "tr": "Meslekler, iş yeri ve okul hakkında konuş, başkalarının ne iş yaptığını söyle."
  },
  "guide": "everest",
  "color": "#1D4ED8",
  "tip": {
    "title": { "en": "She works. Does she work?", "uz": "She works. Does she work?", "ru": "She works. Does she work?", "tr": "She works. Does she work?" },
    "body": {
      "en": "With he, she, it or one person, add -s to the verb: I work, but she works. Study becomes studies, have becomes has. In questions and negatives the -s moves to \"does\" and the verb goes back to its base form: Does she work here? He does not (doesn't) work here. To ask about a job, say: What do you do? What does he do?",
      "uz": "He, she, it yoki bitta odam bilan fe'lga -s qo'shiladi: I work, lekin she works. Study → studies, have → has bo'ladi. Savol va inkorda -s \"does\" ga o'tadi, fe'l esa asl shakliga qaytadi: Does she work here? He does not (doesn't) work here. O'zbek tilida savol -mi, inkor -ma bilan yasaladi, ingliz tilida esa buning uchun alohida \"does\" so'zi kerak. Kasbni so'rash uchun: What do you do? What does he do?",
      "ru": "С he, she, it или одним человеком к глаголу добавляется -s: I work, но she works. Study → studies, have → has. В вопросе и отрицании -s переходит в \"does\", а глагол возвращается в начальную форму: Does she work here? He does not (doesn't) work here. В русском вопрос задаётся интонацией, а в английском нужен \"does\". Чтобы спросить о профессии, говорят: What do you do? What does he do?",
      "tr": "He, she, it ya da tek bir kişiyle fiile -s eklenir: I work, ama she works. Study → studies, have → has olur. Soruda ve olumsuzda -s \"does\" kelimesine geçer, fiil yalın hâline döner: Does she work here? He does not (doesn't) work here. Türkçede soru \"mi\", olumsuzluk \"-me\" ekiyle yapılır; İngilizcede bunun için ayrı bir kelime, \"does\" gerekir. Meslek sormak için: What do you do? What does he do?"
    },
    "examples": [
      { "en": "She works in an office.", "native": { "uz": "U ofisda ishlaydi.", "ru": "Она работает в офисе.", "tr": "O bir ofiste çalışıyor." } },
      { "en": "What does he do?", "native": { "uz": "U nima ish qiladi?", "ru": "Чем он занимается?", "tr": "O ne iş yapıyor?" } },
      { "en": "He does not work at night.", "native": { "uz": "U tunda ishlamaydi.", "ru": "Он не работает ночью.", "tr": "O gece çalışmıyor." } }
    ]
  },
